1. Create migration to add GIN index:
   ```sql
   CREATE INDEX idx_designs_tags ON designs USING GIN (tags);
   ```
2. Update route to use SQL array containment:
   ```typescript
   if (tags) {
     const tagList = tags.split(',').map(t => t.trim().toLowerCase());
     conditions.push(sql`${designs.tags} @> ARRAY[${tagList}]::text[]`);
   }
   ```
3. Apply same pattern to images route for tag filtering
4. Remove post-query JS filtering code

1. Reduce retention from 1000 to 200 entries (sufficient for analytics)
2. Add TTL-based cleanup: discard entries older than 24 hours
3. Implement write batching with debounce:
   ```typescript
   const pendingMetrics: PerformanceMetric[] = [];
   const flushMetrics = debounce(() => {
     const logs = modelMetricsStorage.get('performance_log') || [];
     const updated = [...logs, ...pendingMetrics].slice(-200);
     modelMetricsStorage.set('performance_log', updated);
     pendingMetrics.length = 0;
   }, 5000);

   export const trackModelPerformance = (metric) => {
     pendingMetrics.push({ ...metric, timestamp: Date.now() });
     flushMetrics();
   };
   ```
4. Add cleanup routine on app startup to prune stale entries
5. Consider IndexedDB for async storage if detailed analytics needed
